{
  "id": "versioning-summary",
  "slug": "summary",
  "title": "Summary",
  "category": "Spring Framework",
  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "problem",
      "heading": "Problem:",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "APIs evolve to add new features or fix issues.",
            "Changes can break existing client integrations if not managed carefully."
          ]
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 19,
      "subsections": []
    },
    {
      "id": "real-world-challenge",
      "heading": "Real-World Challenge:",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "If an existing API changes its response structure or behavior, clients depending on the old format may fail."
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 18,
      "subsections": []
    },
    {
      "id": "solution-versioning",
      "heading": "Solution: Versioning",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "Allows APIs to evolve without breaking existing clients.",
            "Enables backward compatibility."
          ]
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 11,
      "subsections": []
    },
    {
      "id": "definition",
      "heading": "Definition:",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "blockquote",
          "text": "Versioning is the practice of managing multiple releases of an API where each version has a similar function but may differ in structure or behavior."
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 25,
      "subsections": []
    },
    {
      "id": "objective",
      "heading": "Objective:",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "Allow clients to migrate to newer versions gradually.",
            "Maintain support for older versions.",
            "Avoid breaking changes for existing users."
          ]
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 19,
      "subsections": []
    },
    {
      "id": "goals-of-versioning",
      "heading": "Goals of Versioning",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Goal",
            "Description"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Backward Compatibility",
              "Ensure old clients continue to work."
            ],
            [
              "Independent Evolution",
              "New features can be added without disrupting existing users."
            ],
            [
              "Client Flexibility",
              "Clients can choose when to adopt a new version."
            ]
          ]
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 32,
      "subsections": []
    },
    {
      "id": "ways-to-achieve-api-versioning",
      "heading": "Ways to Achieve API Versioning",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Spring Boot (and RESTful APIs in general) supports four primary strategies for versioning."
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "URI Versioning (Path Versioning)",
            "Custom Header Versioning",
            "Accept Header (Media Type) Versioning / Content Negotiation",
            "Request Parameter Versioning"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 31,
      "subsections": [
        {
          "id": "description",
          "heading": "Description:",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Version number is included directly in the URL path."
            },
            {
              "type": "image",
              "src": "/Users/luffy/Desktop/Computer Science/Infosys/Spring Rest/Versioning/Versioning/image.png",
              "alt": "image.png",
              "originalPath": "Versioning/image.png"
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 9,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "pros",
          "heading": "Pros:",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "Easy to understand and implement.",
                "Clearly visible and cacheable."
              ]
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 9,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "cons",
          "heading": "Cons:",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "Breaks RESTful principle of resource uniqueness.",
                "Versioning logic tied to URI structure."
              ]
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 12,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "description",
          "heading": "Description:",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Clients send version information using a custom header."
            },
            {
              "type": "image",
              "src": "/Users/luffy/Desktop/Computer Science/Infosys/Spring Rest/Versioning/Versioning/image%201.png",
              "alt": "image.png",
              "originalPath": "Versioning/image%201.png"
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 8,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "pros",
          "heading": "Pros:",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "Keeps URI clean and RESTful.",
                "Allows greater flexibility."
              ]
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 8,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "cons",
          "heading": "Cons:",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "Versioning becomes less visible.",
                "Difficult to test using a browser.",
                "Requires documentation and support from API clients."
              ]
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 17,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "description",
          "heading": "Description:",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Uses Accept HTTP header with a custom media type that includes the version."
            },
            {
              "type": "image",
              "src": "/Users/luffy/Desktop/Computer Science/Infosys/Spring Rest/Versioning/Versioning/image%202.png",
              "alt": "image.png",
              "originalPath": "Versioning/image%202.png"
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 13,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "pros",
          "heading": "Pros:",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "Fully adheres to REST standards (HATEOAS).",
                "Allows fine-grained version control."
              ]
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 10,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "cons",
          "heading": "Cons:",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "Complex to implement and maintain.",
                "Requires content negotiation setup.",
                "Difficult to test using standard tools (like browsers or Postman, unless headers are customized)."
              ]
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 23,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "description",
          "heading": "Description:",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "The version is passed as a query parameter in the request."
            },
            {
              "type": "image",
              "src": "/Users/luffy/Desktop/Computer Science/Infosys/Spring Rest/Versioning/Versioning/image%203.png",
              "alt": "image.png",
              "originalPath": "Versioning/image%203.png"
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 11,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "pros",
          "heading": "Pros:",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "URI structure remains the same.",
                "Easier to route internally via request parameters."
              ]
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 12,
          "subsections": []
        },
        {
          "id": "cons",
          "heading": "Cons:",
          "level": 3,
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "list",
              "ordered": false,
              "items": [
                "Not as intuitive or visible as URI versioning.",
                "Might clutter the query parameters if used excessively."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Method",
                "URI",
                "Header / Param"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "URI Versioning",
                  "/api/v1/customers",
                  "N/A"
                ],
                [
                  "Request Param",
                  "/api/customers?version=1",
                  "N/A"
                ],
                [
                  "Custom Header",
                  "/api/customers",
                  "X-API-VERSION: 1"
                ],
                [
                  "Accept Header",
                  "/api/customers",
                  "Accept: application/vnd.myapp.v1+json"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Versioning Method",
                "URI Structure",
                "Visibility",
                "RESTful",
                "Cache-Friendly",
                "Client Support"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "URI Versioning",
                  "/v1/resource",
                  "High",
                  "Moderate",
                  "Yes",
                  "Easy"
                ],
                [
                  "Param Versioning",
                  "/resource?version=1",
                  "Moderate",
                  "High",
                  "No",
                  "Easy"
                ],
                [
                  "Header Versioning",
                  "/resource + Header",
                  "Low",
                  "High",
                  "Yes",
                  "Hard"
                ],
                [
                  "Accept Header",
                  "/resource + Accept Header",
                  "Low",
                  "High",
                  "Yes",
                  "Hard"
                ]
              ]
            }
          ],
          "wordCount": 81,
          "subsections": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "best-practices-for-api-versioning",
      "heading": "Best Practices for API Versioning",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Practice",
            "Benefit"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Use URI versioning for simple APIs or early-stage projects.",
              "Simplicity and clarity"
            ],
            [
              "Use header-based versioning for enterprise-level APIs.",
              "Flexibility and scalability"
            ],
            [
              "Document versioning strategy clearly.",
              "Helps client developers adopt APIs properly"
            ],
            [
              "Deprecate old versions gracefully.",
              "Encourages migration without breaking clients"
            ],
            [
              "Use semantic versioning if necessary (v1.0, v1.1).",
              "Helps track minor changes"
            ]
          ]
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 53,
      "subsections": []
    },
    {
      "id": "final-thoughts",
      "heading": "Final Thoughts",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Versioning is crucial for API lifecycle management. It empowers developers to:"
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            "Iterate fast",
            "Avoid breaking clients",
            "Communicate upgrades clearly",
            "Design scalable API ecosystems"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "wordCount": 23,
      "subsections": []
    }
  ],
